title: $:/TiddlyDesktop/Settings/MWS
caption: MWS Servers
tags: $:/TiddlyDesktop/Settings

Settings for managing ~MultiWikiServer instances. See [[MWS servers|$:/TiddlyDesktop/Help/MWS]] in the help for details.

!! Node.js folder

~TiddlyDesktop runs `node`, `npm`, `ssh` and `scp` from the system path. If Node.js is installed somewhere else (for example a portable installation), enter the folder that contains the `node` and `npm` executables:

<$edit-text tiddler="$:/TiddlyDesktop/MWS/Config/NodeFolder" class="td-big-textarea" tag="input" placeholder="use the system path"/>

<$button message="tm-mws-check-environment">Check Node.js</$button>
Found: Node.js <$text text={{{ [[$:/temp/TiddlyDesktop/MWS/Environment]get[node]else[not found]] }}}/>, npm <$text text={{{ [[$:/temp/TiddlyDesktop/MWS/Environment]get[npm]else[not found]] }}}/>

!! Backup folder

Backups are stored in a subfolder per server. Leave empty to use the `mws-backups` folder inside the ~TiddlyDesktop configuration folder. Choose a folder on another drive, a NAS or a synchronised cloud folder to protect against disk failure.

<$edit-text tiddler="$:/TiddlyDesktop/MWS/Config/BackupFolder" class="td-big-textarea" tag="input" placeholder="default: mws-backups in the configuration folder"/>

<div class="td-file-input-wrapper">
<$button>Choose folder…</$button>
<$browse nwdirectory message="tm-mws-pick-folder" param="$:/TiddlyDesktop/MWS/Config/BackupFolder!!text"/>
</div>
<$button>
<$action-deletetiddler $tiddler="$:/TiddlyDesktop/MWS/Config/BackupFolder"/>
Reset to default
</$button>
